  "result": "All 243 tests pass now. Two tests had been failing, and they came from two separate bugs:\n\n1. **Wrong order in `src/cart.js`:** `total()` added tax first and then took the discount off. The comment in the code says the discount should come off the pre-tax subtotal. For percent discounts the order makes no difference, which is why all the percent tests passed. For fixed discounts it does: 100 − 20 = 80, then 10% tax gives 88. The code was giving 110 − 20 = 90. I swapped it so the discount comes off first and tax is added after.\n2. **Negative totals in `src/discount.js`:** a fixed discount bigger than the subtotal could push the total below zero (−14.5 in the test). It now stops at 0 (`Math.max(0, amount - discount.value)`), which matches the \"never below zero\" rule in that same comment.\n\nI didn't change any tests.",
